{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793807961,"nonce":"rsKXlIgyFiQI2K6YFxUszhK2xy8=","title":"OSR: preserve proven receiver facts when outlining from lowered interpreter frames","message":"Interpreter-first static-hot dispatch (tracked in c88912cc2fdd3b761b803421ad6caaec30cf2770ccd1171d667c44661aa8b743) exposes a native-code-quality gap in the region entered by the running method_call frame. Removing the first-call compile wait allows correct execution and actual interpreter-to-Cranelift OSR, but the region receives the Toggle receiver as an ordinary pointer parameter. The whole-function optimizer previously saw its construction/allocation.\n\nObserved in /private/tmp/zyntax-interp-first/hir/fn-lua_chunk_resume1-outlined-opt.hir and dump.trace: the first loop again contains ten state load/XOR/store sequences and a receiver null check. The whole-function Cranelift path after dfc3eda54f4e8907cb33e0fc1cd3c6de9f5129b2 has one XOR and two stores, retaining the cold-exit store. The outlined function keeps source-line global stores between receiver accesses. Its ordinary live-in parameter no longer supplies the fresh-allocation-versus-global disjointness used by scalar store forwarding. osr::outline currently carries release ownership but not the relevant receiver provenance/refinements.\n\nNUC paired medians, 11 samples per arm, frozen binary, cool/idle gates, no cargo/rustc: Cranelift-only short wall 29.138 -\u003e 29.048 ms; long wall 46.767 -\u003e 53.830 ms (+15.1%). LLVM-enabled short 30.405 -\u003e 31.306 ms; long 49.812 -\u003e 56.383 ms (+13.2%). Internal os.clock intervals are not directly comparable because execution now reaches the timer before background compilation finishes. All target outputs match. Additional five-pair experiment disabling static-hot precompile through a getenv shim preserving the native snapshot: short 29.170 -\u003e 28.927 ms, long 54.426 -\u003e 52.066 ms; removing speculation alone does not recover the old long-run speed.\n\nCarry only proven source-frame facts into the outlined region, or establish guarded refinements at its entry. Preserve aliasing between live-ins, cold-exit state, source positions and null/error semantics. Do not mark all pointer live-ins noalias: multiple live-ins can name the same object. Verify HIR and final machine code, actual OSR, alias/null adversarial tests, full pinned TS corpus and NUC timings. This remains a separate optimization task; do not restore the blocking interpreter bypass to conceal it.","files":null}]}